<button
  type="button"
  data-sierra-nevada-difficulty-open
  class="flex min-h-12 w-full items-center justify-center rounded-lg border-2 border-transparent bg-[#ff5e00] px-5 py-3 text-lg font-bold text-white shadow-lg shadow-[#ff5e00]/25 transition-colors hover:bg-[#3c5546] focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-[#3c5546]">
  Difficulty Levels
</button>

<dialog
  data-sierra-nevada-difficulty-dialog
  aria-labelledby="sierra-nevada-difficulty-title"
  class="m-auto max-h-[calc(100vh-2rem)] w-[calc(100%-2rem)] max-w-5xl overflow-hidden rounded-lg border-0 bg-white p-0 text-[#233229] shadow-2xl backdrop:bg-black/60">
  <div class="flex max-h-[calc(100vh-2rem)] flex-col">
    <header
      class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4 bg-[#3c5546] px-5 py-4 text-white sm:px-8">
      <div>
        <p class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-[#ffbe8f]">
          Sierra Nevada E-MTB Tour
        </p>
        <h2
          id="sierra-nevada-difficulty-title"
          class="mt-1 text-2xl font-bold sm:text-3xl">
          Difficulty Levels
        </h2>
      </div>
      <form method="dialog">
        <button
          type="submit"
          class="rounded-lg border border-white/60 px-3 py-2 text-sm font-bold transition-colors hover:bg-white hover:text-[#3c5546] focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-[#ff5e00]">
          Close
        </button>
      </form>
    </header>

    <div class="overflow-y-auto px-5 py-6 sm:px-8 sm:py-8">
      <article
        class="border border-[#3c5546]/20 border-l-4 border-l-[#ff5e00] p-5">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#3c5546]">
          Trail Difficulty Rating System
        </h3>
        <h4 class="mt-2 text-lg font-bold text-[#3c5546]">
          Technical Level: S0 - S1 (Easy to Moderate)
        </h4>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          This tour is designed for a wide range of riders, making it an
          excellent choice for anyone with a reasonable level of fitness and
          some basic mountain biking experience.
        </p>

        <section class="mt-5 border-t border-[#3c5546]/15 pt-4">
          <h4 class="font-bold text-[#3c5546]">S0</h4>
          <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
            S0 indicates a single trail that does not present particular
            difficulties. Most of them are forest or meadow trails with good
            grip, or compact gravel. In this type of trails you will not face
            steps, rocks or roots. The gradient of the trail goes from mild to
            moderate and the curves are always quite wide. S0 trails can be
            tackled without special mountain bike technical skills.
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 leading-relaxed">
            <li><strong>Trail conditions:</strong> compact terrain with good grip</li>
            <li><strong>Obstacles:</strong> none</li>
            <li><strong>Gradient:</strong> mild to moderate</li>
            <li><strong>Curves:</strong> wide</li>
            <li><strong>MTB Tech Skills:</strong> no special skills required</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
            We include the double track with rides on hard-pack gravel/dirt. The
            doubletrack is relatively wide where you can cycle side by side and
            offer a more social riding experience, perfect for enjoying the
            scenery together.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mt-5 border-t border-[#3c5546]/15 pt-4">
          <h4 class="font-bold text-[#3c5546]">S1</h4>
          <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
            On an S1 trail you will find small obstacles such as not very
            prominent roots and small stones. Often the increased difficulty
            rating is due to the drains or erosion. In S1 single trails the
            surface could be not very compact. The gradient reaches a maximum
            of 40% and no switchbacks will be encountered. Starting from S1
            level, basic mtb riding techniques and good concentration are
            required. The trickier passages require the ability to dose the
            brakes and to affect the trajectory by body displacement. Obstacles
            can all be rolled over with basic riding skills.
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 leading-relaxed">
            <li>
              <strong>Trail conditions:</strong> loose surface possible, with
              small roots and stones
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Obstacles:</strong> small obstacles (drains, damage caused
              by erosion)
            </li>
            <li><strong>Gradient:</strong> &lt;40%</li>
            <li><strong>Curves:</strong> narrow</li>
            <li>
              <strong>MTB Tech skills:</strong> basic driving skills required
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</dialog>

<script>
  const openButton = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>(
    "[data-sierra-nevada-difficulty-open]",
  );
  const dialog = document.querySelector<HTMLDialogElement>(
    "[data-sierra-nevada-difficulty-dialog]",
  );

  openButton?.addEventListener("click", () => dialog?.showModal());

  dialog?.addEventListener("click", (event) => {
    if (event.target === dialog) {
      dialog.close();
    }
  });
</script>
